Description: Move a window maximized or fullscreen before its session restore to the monitor of its stored state.
 A client can request being maximized or fullscreen before it restores its toplevel, and GTK does so for a window it
 restores maximized. Mutter then maximizes the window on the monitor it was created on before restoring it, and
 restoring it sets its target monitor and maximizes it again, which leaves it where it is. A Ptyxis window saved
 maximized on a second monitor returned maximized on the first one, also with restore-target-monitor.patch.
 .
 Restoring now moves a window which already is maximized or fullscreen to the monitor of its stored state.
 .
 The test restore-maximized-other-workspace-client-maximized restores a window maximized on a second monitor, whose
 client requests being maximized before it restores its toplevel, and fails without the change, as the window is
 maximized on the first monitor.
Author: Mitar
Last-Update: 2026-11-16
